// test-error
// ADR-003 / #1306 review: a dynamic memory import reports ONCE.
//
// This form used to report twice for the single call below -- once from the
// declaration listener scanning statement text, once from the postfix listener
// seeing the call. Every committed fixture was a bare statement, the one shape
// that reported once, so the duplicate was invisible.
//
// NEGATIVE CONTROL: `abs` is also imported from stdlib.h and must stay silent.
// A change that rejected every stdlib import would pass without it.
#include <stdlib.h>

void allocateAndStore() {
    u32 kept <- abs(-5);
    u32 block <- malloc(64);
}
